Package: supershot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: @SHLIBDEPS@
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-kde | xdg-desktop-portal-wlr | xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
Suggests: grim, slurp, gnome-screenshot, scrot
Maintainer: axpnet <axp@pm.me>
Homepage: https://github.com/axpnet/supershot
Description: GTK4/Libadwaita screenshot tool with annotation and redaction
 SuperShot is a native GTK4/Libadwaita screenshot tool for Linux desktops.
 It captures through the XDG Desktop Portal on both Wayland and X11, and
 falls back to the session's own command-line tools (grim/slurp, spectacle,
 gnome-screenshot, xfce4-screenshooter, scrot, maim, flameshot) when no
 portal backend is available.
 .
 Features an annotation toolbar (arrow, rectangle, ellipse, highlighter,
 free draw, text, numbered steps), pixelate and blackout redaction that
 destroys the underlying pixels rather than covering them, crop, an image
 editor (rotate, flip, brightness, contrast, blur, sharpen, grayscale,
 invert), a customisable date/time watermark, PNG and JPEG output with
 configurable quality, clipboard export, desktop notifications, a CLI
 headless mode for scripting, and 14 language translations.
